## Plain-English Summary

Analysts can only review a fraction of the alerts a rule-based monitoring system raises. This model does not decide which alerts fire - the five rule scenarios (STR-01, RMV-01, FAN-01, FAN-02, WLT-01) do that, at their Phase 5 chosen thresholds, unchanged. **{{ rules[0] }}**

What the model does is rank the queue so the alerts most likely to be genuine (productive) are reviewed first. On the test period, reviewing the top 20% of the queue in model order catches {{ budget_20.captured.xgboost }} of {{ test_n_positives }} productive alerts - compared to {{ budget_20.captured.fifo }} for first-in-first-out order and {{ budget_20.captured.random_mean }} for random order over the same budget.

## 1. Purpose and Scope

This model reorders the combined alert queue from all five scenarios; it is evaluated against three baselines: a logistic regression on the same features, a "scenario prior" (rank by each scenario's own historical productive rate, no per-alert learning at all), and the FIFO/random orders an analyst queue would otherwise use.

